`git apply --check` passes against ce8f85a26. Validation with the overlay first on sys.path
(scratch venv with the `test` group + duckdb/sqlglot/pandas/polars/pyarrow):
  - tests/_runtime (whole directory), tests/test_entrypoints.py, tests/_sql, tests/_data,
    tests/_ast/test_cell.py, tests/_ast/test_sql_visitor.py: 2854 passed, 4 failed.
    The 4 failures are not caused by the diff: 3x tests/_data/test_preview_column.py
    ::test_preview_column_duration_dtype also fail on the unmodified tree in that venv, and
    tests/_runtime/test_pytest_runtime.py::test_offline_collection_inside_marimo_package
    writes into marimo/_smoke_tests/, which the overlay copy omits (passes on the real tree).
  - identical per-cell notification streams for smoke/outputs/chain-100
    (.context/perf/backend-runtime/check_parity.py)
  - tests/_runtime/test_large_notebook.py: chain-240 run-all 2.49M -> 0.73M function
    calls, run-one-leaf 185.7k -> 9.6k; smoke-240 run-one-leaf 39.3k -> 13.6k

Hunks by finding (see .context/perf/backend-runtime.md):
  F1  lazy startup: reuse compiled pending cells instead of recompiling them per run request
        _runtime/runtime.py (StartupCellCache.peek, prepare_execution_requests)
  F3  duckdb datasource hook: `imported()` instead of `has()`; reuse the parsed module for `sqls`
        _runtime/runner/hooks_post_execution.py, _ast/cell.py
  F4  resolve the cell executor once per kernel
        _runtime/runner/cell_runner.py (executor param), _runtime/runtime.py (_resolve_executor)
  F5  module-registry scan once per graph mutation instead of twice per invalidated cell
        _runtime/runtime.py (_invalidate_cell_state, mutate_graph)
  F6  index python references per name (O(1) get_referring_cells)
        _runtime/dataflow/topology.py, _runtime/dataflow/edges.py, _runtime/dataflow/graph.py
  F7  one traversal for "which cells are disabled" per run; early-exit ancestor checks;
      dispose descendants once per run
        _runtime/dataflow/graph.py, _runtime/runner/hooks_preparation.py,
        _runtime/runner/cell_runner.py, _runtime/runtime.py
  F9  state registry: predicate instead of a per-cell union of every name
        _runtime/runner/hooks_post_execution.py, _runtime/state.py

Not in this diff (prototyped by monkeypatch in .context/perf/backend-runtime/patches.py):
  F2  reuse one stdout/stderr pipe + reader thread across cells (apply_redirect_reuse)
  F8  autoreload: coalesce the per-cell sys.modules scan (apply_autoreload_coalesce)
  F12 skip the console flush round-trip when nothing was written (apply_flush_skip)
  F6  linear-time stale/disabled-ancestor checks at registration (apply_disabled_counter)

